note ===== flog.om : IEEE f64 fused multiply-add in integer arithmetic, and natural log =====
note Owner FtsEngine. Globals q*, functions flog*.
note API
note   flog_init        decode the glibc table once (fts_init calls it)
note   flog_fma a b c   = RN(a*b+c) with one rounding, the AArch64 FMADD result, for finite
note                    operands (any normal, subnormal or zero); an inf or NaN operand falls
note                    back to (a*b)+c with two roundings
note   flog x           = bit-exact replica of glibc 2.39 aarch64 log (libm.so.6 sha256
note                    5e039156...1b4a, log@@GLIBC_2.29 at 0x34cd0): same table, same
note                    operation order, same fused operations (see evidence/fts/glibc-log.dis)
note glibc's log is not correctly rounded (bound 0.519 ulp), so a correctly rounded log would
note not bit-match it; this file replicates the glibc instruction sequence instead.
note scratch for 128-bit values: qfh:qfl
global qfh ulong 1
global qfl ulong 1
note decoded __log_data: 0 ln2hi, 1 ln2lo, 2..6 poly A0..A4, 7..17 poly1 B0..B10, 18+2i invc, 19+2i logc
global qlgt ulong 274
global qlgi ulong 1
